preserved in a brine solution usually containing sulfur dioxide and calcium chloride to bleach the fruit, then soaked in a suspension of food coloring (common red food dye is Allura Red AC), sugar syrup, and other components. The name and the original fruit is indigenous to Croatia (Croatian: višnja maraska or višnja maraske), originally a luxury delicacy of the  Dalmatian Coast, specifically Zadar, these cherries were dark, sour, and pitted before being steeped in a spirit distilled from the fruit’s own pits, skins, and leaves."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-maraschino-cherry"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maraschino_cherry"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["English cuisine","cuisine/english-cuisine",[["Manchester tart","dish/manchester-tart"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Coconut","ingredient/coconut"],["Custard","ingredient/custard"],["Fruit preserves","ingredient/fruit-preserves"],["Shortcrust pastry","ingredient/shortcrust-pastry"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/b/bd/Real_maraschino_cherries.jpg/500px-Real_maraschino_cherries.jpg","w":500,"h":625,"by":"Ilikefood","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Real_maraschino_cherries.jpg"}},"dish/mett":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/mett","n":"Mett","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Mett, also known as Hackepeter (Northern Germany, Eastern Germany and Berlin), is a preparation of minced raw pork seasoned with salt and black pepper that is popular in Germany. It is frequently spread on halves of a bread roll, with raw onion optionally on top. Since the 1950s mett has also been offered as a buffet dish decoratively formed into the shape of a hedgehog, with raw onion \"spines\". German law forbids mett being sold with a fat content exceeding 35%."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-mett"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mett"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["German cuisine","cuisine/german-cuisine"],["Thuringian cuisine","cuisine/german-cuisine-thuringia"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Quick German Recipes","ref":"site/quick-german-recipes-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"quick-german-recipes.com","note":"Long-running site by German-born cook Gerhild Fulson (Oma) with traditional German home recipes.","url":"https://www.quick-german-recipes.com/about-me.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Dirndl Kitchen","ref":"site/dirndlkitchen-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dirndlkitchen.com","note":"Blog of German and Bavarian recipes, from main dishes to holiday baking.","url":"https://dirndlkitchen.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Quick German Recipes","ref":"site/quick-german-recipes-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"quick-german-recipes.com","note":"Thuringia page on German-born cook Gerhild Fulson's long-running German recipe site.","url":"https://www.quick-german-recipes.com/thuringia.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from German cuisine","links":[["Baumkuchen","dish/baumkuchen"],["Berlin Inn","dish/berlin-inn"],["Bockwurst","dish/bockwurst"],["Buchteln","dish/buchteln"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Chrain","dish/chrain"],["Dampfnudel","dish/dampfnudel"],["Der Rheinlander","dish/der-rheinlander"],["Eel soup","dish/eel-soup"],["Egg puffs and soup pearls","dish/egg-puffs-and-soup-pearls"],["Eintopf","dish/eintopf"],["Flammekueche","dish/flammekueche"],["Gugelhupf","dish/gugelhupf"],["Hamburg steak","dish/hamburg-steak"],["Hedgehog slice","dish/hedgehog-slice"],["Herman ze German","dish/herman-ze-german"],["Horcher (restaurant)","dish/horcher-restaurant"],["Kringle","dish/kringle"],["Labskaus","dish/labskaus"],["Landjäger","dish/landjager"],["Leberkäse","dish/leberkase"],["Mock turtle so